[2026-03-14T20:56:10.033Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RYY5KaMwMRMFNY9AXcdady","type":"tool_result","content":"   747→## Page: Host Dashboard (`/hosting`)\n   748→\n   749→<!-- Components: StatsOverview, ListingsTab, BookingsTab, AddListingForm -->\n   750→\n   751→### Component: StatsOverview\n   752→\n   753→#### Test: Host Dashboard requires login — redirects unauthenticated users\n   754→- **Initial state:** No user is logged in.\n   755→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   756→- **Expected:** The app redirects the user to `/login`. The Host Dashboard is not rendered.\n   757→\n   758→#### Test: Host Dashboard requires host status — shows upgrade prompt for non-hosts\n   759→- **Initial state:** A user is logged in with `is_host` set to false.\n   760→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   761→- **Expected:** The page displays a message indicating the user is not a host (e.g., \"You need to become a host to access this page\") with a link or button to navigate to their profile page (`/profile`) where they can become a host.\n   762→\n   763→#### Test: Stats overview displays total listings count\n   764→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with 5 active properties and 1 inactive property in the database.\n   765→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   766→- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays a \"Total Listings\" stat card showing \"5\" (only active listings counted). The card has a label \"Total Listings\" and a numeric value.\n   767→\n   768→#### Test: Stats overview displays active bookings count\n   769→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have 3 bookings with status \"confirmed\", 2 with status \"pending\", and 4 with status \"completed\".\n   770→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   771→- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays an \"Active Bookings\" stat card showing \"5\" (pending + confirmed bookings). The card has a label \"Active Bookings\" and a numeric value.\n   772→\n   773→#### Test: Stats overview displays total earnings\n   774→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have completed bookings with total_price values of $500, $750, and $1200.\n   775→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   776→- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays a \"Total Earnings\" stat card showing \"$2,450\" (sum of completed booking total prices). The value is formatted as currency.\n   777→\n   778→#### Test: Stats overview displays average rating\n   779→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have reviews with overall ratings of 4, 5, 3, and 5.\n   780→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   781→- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays an \"Average Rating\" stat card showing \"4.3\" (average of all review ratings, rounded to one decimal). A star icon is displayed next to the value.\n   782→\n   783→#### Test: Stats overview shows zeros for a new host with no data\n   784→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with no properties, no bookings, and no reviews.\n   785→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   786→- **Expected:** All four stat cards display zero/empty values: \"Total Listings: 0\", \"Active Bookings: 0\", \"Total Earnings: $0\", and \"Average Rating: —\" (or \"N/A\" when no reviews exist).\n   787→\n   788→#### Test: Host Dashboard displays navigation tabs for Listings and Bookings\n   789→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host.\n   790→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   791→- **Expected:** Below the stats overview, two tabs are visible: \"Listings\" and \"Bookings\". The \"Listings\" tab is active/selected by default.\n   792→\n   793→#### Test: Switching between Listings and Bookings tabs\n   794→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host and on `/hosting` with the \"Listings\" tab active.\n   795→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Bookings\" tab.\n   796→- **Expected:** The Bookings tab content is displayed (table of bookings). The \"Bookings\" tab appears active/selected. User clicks \"Listings\" tab again and the listings grid is displayed.\n   797→\n   798→### Component: ListingsTab\n   799→\n   800→#### Test: Listings tab displays host's properties in a grid\n   801→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with 3 active properties: \"Beach House\" ($150/night), \"Mountain Cabin\" ($200/night), \"City Loft\" ($120/night).\n   802→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting` (Listings tab is active by default).\n   803→- **Expected:** A grid of 3 property cards is displayed. Each card shows the property title, main image, price per night, and status (active/inactive).\n   804→\n   805→#### Test: Listing card shows property details\n   806→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with a property: title \"Beach House\", price $150/night, city \"Malibu\", 4.5 average rating, 10 reviews, active status.\n   807→- **Expected:** The listing card displays the property title \"Beach House\", price \"$150/night\", location \"Malibu\", average rating \"4.5\" with star icon, review count \"10 reviews\", and a green \"Active\" badge.\n   808→\n   809→#### Test: Listing card has Edit button that navigates to property detail\n   810→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with a property (id \"prop-123\").\n   811→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Edit\" button on the property card.\n   812→- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/properties/prop-123` where the host can view and edit their property details.\n   813→\n   814→#### Test: Listing card has Deactivate button for active properties\n   815→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with an active property \"Beach House\".\n   816→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Deactivate\" button on the \"Beach House\" card.\n   817→- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears asking \"Are you sure you want to deactivate this listing?\". The dialog shows the property name \"Beach House\".\n   818→\n   819→#### Test: Confirming deactivation sets property to inactive\n   820→- **Initial state:** The deactivation confirmation dialog is open for \"Beach House\".\n   821→- **Action:** User clicks the confirm button (e.g., \"Yes, Deactivate\").\n   822→- **Expected:** The app calls `DELETE /api/properties/:id` (which sets `is_active` to false). The dialog closes. The property card updates to show an \"Inactive\" status badge (gray or muted). A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Listing deactivated\"). The stats overview updates the \"Total Listings\" count to reflect the change.\n   823→\n   824→#### Test: Dismissing deactivation dialog keeps property active\n   825→- **Initial state:** The deactivation confirmation dialog is open for \"Beach House\".\n   826→- **Action:** User clicks the dismiss/cancel button.\n   827→- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The property remains active with no changes.\n   828→\n   829→#### Test: Listing card shows Activate button for inactive properties\n   830→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with an inactive property \"Old Cabin\".\n   831→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Activate\" button on the \"Old Cabin\" card.\n   832→- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/properties/:id` to set `is_active` to true. The property card updates to show a green \"Active\" badge. The \"Total Listings\" stat updates.\n   833→\n   834→#### Test: Listings tab shows empty state for host with no properties\n   835→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with no properties.\n   836→- **Expected:** The Listings tab displays an empty state message (e.g., \"You don't have any listings yet\") and a prominent \"Add Listing\" button or call-to-action.\n   837→\n   838→#### Test: Add Listing button is visible on the Listings tab\n   839→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host.\n   840→- **Expected:** An \"Add Listing\" button is prominently displayed on the Listings tab (e.g., in the header area or as a floating action button). The button has clear text \"Add Listing\" or a \"+\" icon with label.\n   841→\n   842→#### Test: Deactivate and activate actions work on repeated use\n   843→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with two active properties.\n   844→- **Action:** User deactivates the first property (confirms dialog), then activates it again, then deactivates the second property.\n   845→- **Expected:** Each action updates the correct property's status. The stats overview correctly reflects the current count of active listings after each action.\n   846→\n   847→### Component: BookingsTab\n   848→\n   849→#### Test: Bookings tab displays table of bookings for host's properties\n   850→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have bookings from various guests.\n   851→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Bookings\" tab.\n   852→- **Expected:** A table is displayed with columns: Property, Guest, Check-in, Check-out, Guests, Total, Status, and Actions. Each booking is a row in the table.\n   853→\n   854→#### Test: Bookings table shows correct data for each booking\n   855→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. A booking exists: property \"Beach House\", guest \"Alice Smith\", check-in \"2026-07-01\", check-out \"2026-07-05\", 2 guests, total $750, status \"confirmed\".\n   856→- **Expected:** The table row displays: \"Beach House\", \"Alice Smith\", \"Jul 1, 2026\", \"Jul 5, 2026\", \"2\", \"$750\", a green \"Confirmed\" status badge.\n   857→\n   858→#### Test: Bookings tab has status filter controls\n   859→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab.\n   860→- **Expected:** Filter controls are visible above the table allowing the host to filter by status: \"All\", \"Pending\", \"Confirmed\", \"Cancelled\", \"Completed\". \"All\" is selected by default.\n   861→\n   862→#### Test: Filtering bookings by Pending status\n   863→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. Bookings exist with statuses \"pending\", \"confirmed\", and \"completed\".\n   864→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Pending\" status filter.\n   865→- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"pending\" are displayed in the table. The \"Pending\" filter appears active/selected.\n   866→\n   867→#### Test: Filtering bookings by Confirmed status\n   868→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n   869→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Confirmed\" status filter.\n   870→- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"confirmed\" are shown. Other bookings are hidden.\n   871→\n   872→#### Test: Filtering bookings by Completed status\n   873→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n   874→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Completed\" status filter.\n   875→- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"completed\" are shown.\n   876→\n   877→#### Test: Filtering bookings by Cancelled status\n   878→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n   879→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancelled\" status filter.\n   880→- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"cancelled\" are shown.\n   881→\n   882→#### Test: Resetting filter to All shows all bookings\n   883→- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with the \"Pending\" filter active.\n   884→- **Action:** User clicks the \"All\" filter.\n   885→- **Expected:** All bookings across all statuses are displayed again.\n   886→\n   887→#### Test: Status filters work on repeated use\n   888→- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n   889→- **Action:** User clicks \"Pending\", then \"Confirmed\", then \"All\", then \"Completed\".\n   890→- **Expected:** Each filter correctly shows the appropriate subset of bookings. The active filter indicator updates correctly each time.\n   891→\n   892→#### Test: Host can confirm a pending booking\n   893→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. A booking with status \"pending\" for guest \"Bob\" at property \"Beach House\" is displayed.\n   894→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Confirm\" button on that booking row.\n   895→- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"confirmed\". The booking's status badge changes from yellow \"Pending\" to green \"Confirmed\". The \"Confirm\" button is no longer visible for that booking. A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Booking confirmed\"). The \"Active Bookings\" stat in StatsOverview remains accurate.\n   896→\n   897→#### Test: Host can cancel a pending booking\n   898→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. A pending booking is displayed.\n   899→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the pending booking row.\n   900→- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears asking the host to confirm cancellation. The dialog shows the guest name, property, and dates for context.\n   901→\n   902→#### Test: Confirming cancellation of a booking updates status\n   903→- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a pending booking.\n   904→- **Action:** User clicks the confirm button in the dialog.\n   905→- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"cancelled\". The dialog closes. The booking's status badge changes to red \"Cancelled\". The \"Cancel\" and \"Confirm\" action buttons are removed for that booking. A success message is displayed. The \"Active Bookings\" stat decreases by 1.\n   906→\n   907→#### Test: Dismissing booking cancellation dialog keeps booking unchanged\n   908→- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a booking.\n   909→- **Action:** User clicks the dismiss button or clicks outside the dialog.\n   910→- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The booking status remains unchanged.\n   911→\n   912→#### Test: Host can cancel a confirmed booking\n   913→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. A booking with status \"confirmed\" is displayed.\n   914→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the confirmed booking row and confirms in the dialog.\n   915→- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"cancelled\". The status badge changes to red \"Cancelled\". The \"Active Bookings\" stat decreases.\n   916→\n   917→#### Test: Completed and cancelled bookings have no action buttons\n   918→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. Bookings exist with statuses \"completed\" and \"cancelled\".\n   919→- **Expected:** Booking rows with \"completed\" or \"cancelled\" status do not display \"Confirm\" or \"Cancel\" action buttons. Only pending and confirmed bookings show action buttons.\n   920→\n   921→#### Test: Bookings tab shows empty state when no bookings exist\n   922→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with properties but no bookings.\n   923→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Bookings\" tab.\n   924→- **Expected:** The tab displays an empty state message (e.g., \"No bookings yet\").\n   925→\n   926→#### Test: Status badges display correct colors\n   927→- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with bookings in all four statuses.\n   928→- **Expected:** Status badges use the correct colors: \"Pending\" has a yellow badge, \"Confirmed\" has a green badge, \"Cancelled\" has a red badge, \"Completed\" has a blue badge.\n   929→\n   930→#### Test: Confirm and cancel actions work on repeated use\n   931→- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with three pending bookings.\n   932→- **Action:** User confirms the first booking, cancels the second booking (confirming the dialog), and then confirms the third booking.\n   933→- **Expected:** Each action updates the correct booking. The first and third show \"Confirmed\" badges, the second shows \"Cancelled\". Stats update correctly after each action.\n   934→\n   935→### Component: AddListingForm\n   936→\n   937→#### Test: Clicking Add Listing button opens the multi-step form\n   938→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Listings tab.\n   939→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Add Listing\" button.\n   940→- **Expected:** A multi-step form opens (modal or full-page). Step 1 is displayed with fields for property type and title. A step indicator shows progress (Step 1 of 7). \"Next\" and \"Cancel\" buttons are visible.\n   941→\n   942→#### Test: Step 1 — Property type selection and title input\n   943→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is open on Step 1.\n   944→- **Expected:** A dropdown or selection control lists property types: \"Apartment\", \"House\", \"Cabin\", \"Villa\", \"Condo\", \"Loft\", \"Cottage\", \"Townhouse\". A text input field for the property title is visible. Both fields are required.\n   945→\n   946→#### Test: Step 1 — Selecting property type and entering title\n   947→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 1.\n   948→- **Action:** User selects \"Cabin\" from the property type selector and types \"Cozy Mountain Retreat\" in the title field.\n   949→- **Expected:** The property type shows \"Cabin\" selected. The title field displays \"Cozy Mountain Retreat\". The \"Next\" button becomes enabled (or was already enabled).\n   950→\n   951→#### Test: Step 1 — Validation prevents proceeding without required fields\n   952→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 1 with no selections made.\n   953→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\" without selecting a property type or entering a title.\n   954→- **Expected:** Validation errors are displayed for both fields (e.g., \"Property type is required\", \"Title is required\"). The form does not advance to Step 2.\n   955→\n   956→#### Test: Step 2 — Location fields displayed\n   957→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 1 and clicked \"Next\".\n   958→- **Expected:** Step 2 is displayed with fields for: address (with geocoding/autocomplete), city, state, and country. A \"Back\" button and \"Next\" button are visible. The step indicator shows Step 2 of 7.\n   959→\n   960→#### Test: Step 2 — Address field uses autocomplete\n   961→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 2.\n   962→- **Action:** User types \"123 Main\" in the address field.\n   963→- **Expected:** An autocomplete dropdown appears with address suggestions from a geocoding API (e.g., OpenStreetMap Nominatim). Selecting a suggestion populates the address field with the full address.\n   964→\n   965→#### Test: Step 2 — Address autocomplete populates related fields\n   966→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 2.\n   967→- **Action:** User types in the address field and selects an autocomplete suggestion for \"123 Main St, Denver, CO, USA\".\n   968→- **Expected:** The address field is populated with \"123 Main St\". The city field is auto-filled with \"Denver\". The state field is auto-filled with \"CO\". The country field is auto-filled with \"USA\".\n   969→\n   970→#### Test: Step 2 — Validation requires city and country\n   971→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 2 with address filled but city and country empty.\n   972→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n   973→- **Expected:** Validation errors appear for city and country (e.g., \"City is required\", \"Country is required\"). The form does not advance.\n   974→\n   975→#### Test: Step 3 — Details fields displayed\n   976→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 2 and clicked \"Next\".\n   977→- **Expected:** Step 3 is displayed with numeric input fields for: max guests, bedrooms, beds, and bathrooms. Each field has increment/decrement controls or is a number input. The step indicator shows Step 3 of 7.\n   978→\n   979→#### Test: Step 3 — Setting property details\n   980→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 3.\n   981→- **Action:** User sets max guests to 4, bedrooms to 2, beds to 3, bathrooms to 1.\n   982→- **Expected:** All fields display the entered values. The \"Next\" button is enabled.\n   983→\n   984→#### Test: Step 3 — Validation requires all detail fields\n   985→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 3 with all fields at 0 or empty.\n   986→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n   987→- **Expected:** Validation errors appear (e.g., \"Max guests must be at least 1\"). The form does not advance.\n   988→\n   989→#### Test: Step 4 — Amenities selection displayed\n   990→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 3 and clicked \"Next\".\n   991→- **Expected:** Step 4 is displayed with checkboxes for amenities grouped by category: \"Essentials\", \"Features\", \"Safety\", \"Location\". Each category heading is visible with its amenities listed below. The step indicator shows Step 4 of 7.\n   992→\n   993→#### Test: Step 4 — Selecting amenities\n   994→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 4 with amenities loaded from `GET /api/amenities`.\n   995→- **Action:** User checks \"WiFi\" and \"Kitchen\" under Essentials, and \"Pool\" under Features.\n   996→- **Expected:** The selected amenities show as checked. The user can proceed to the next step. Amenities are optional (no validation error if none selected).\n   997→\n   998→#### Test: Step 4 — Amenities are toggleable\n   999→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 4 with \"WiFi\" already checked.\n  1000→- **Action:** User clicks \"WiFi\" to uncheck it, then checks it again.\n  1001→- **Expected:** The checkbox toggles correctly on each click.\n  1002→\n  1003→#### Test: Step 5 — Photo URL input displayed\n  1004→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 4 and clicked \"Next\".\n  1005→- **Expected:** Step 5 is displayed with an input field for image URLs and an \"Add Photo\" button. A list/grid of added photos is shown below (initially empty). The step indicator shows Step 5 of 7.\n  1006→\n  1007→#### Test: Step 5 — Adding a photo URL\n  1008→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 5.\n  1009→- **Action:** User types \"https://example.com/photo1.jpg\" in the URL input and clicks \"Add Photo\".\n  1010→- **Expected:** The photo URL is added to the list. A preview or thumbnail of the image is displayed. The URL input is cleared for the next entry. An optional caption field may be shown for the added photo.\n  1011→\n  1012→#### Test: Step 5 — Adding multiple photo URLs\n  1013→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 5 with one photo already added.\n  1014→- **Action:** User adds two more photo URLs.\n  1015→- **Expected:** All three photos are displayed in the list/grid. Each photo can be reordered or removed.\n  1016→\n  1017→#### Test: Step 5 — Removing a photo\n  1018→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 5 with 3 photos added.\n  1019→- **Action:** User clicks the remove/delete button on the second photo.\n  1020→- **Expected:** The second photo is removed from the list. The remaining 2 photos are displayed.\n  1021→\n  1022→#### Test: Step 5 — Validation requires at least one photo\n  1023→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 5 with no photos added.\n  1024→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n  1025→- **Expected:** A validation error appears (e.g., \"At least one photo is required\"). The form does not advance.\n  1026→\n  1027→#### Test: Step 6 — Pricing fields displayed\n  1028→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 5 and clicked \"Next\".\n  1029→- **Expected:** Step 6 is displayed with numeric input fields for: price per night and cleaning fee. The price per night field is required. The cleaning fee defaults to 0. Currency formatting or prefix ($) is shown. The step indicator shows Step 6 of 7.\n  1030→\n  1031→#### Test: Step 6 — Entering pricing information\n  1032→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 6.\n  1033→- **Action:** User enters 150 for price per night and 50 for cleaning fee.\n  1034→- **Expected:** The fields display $150 and $50 respectively.\n  1035→\n  1036→#### Test: Step 6 — Validation requires price per night\n  1037→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 6 with price per night empty or 0.\n  1038→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n  1039→- **Expected:** A validation error appears (e.g., \"Price per night is required and must be greater than 0\"). The form does not advance.\n  1040→\n  1041→#### Test: Step 7 — Review and publish page displayed\n  1042→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 6 and clicked \"Next\".\n  1043→- **Expected:** Step 7 displays a summary of all entered information: property type, title, full address (address, city, state, country), details (guests, bedrooms, beds, bathrooms), selected amenities, photo thumbnails, price per night, and cleaning fee. A \"Publish\" button and \"Back\" button are visible. The step indicator shows Step 7 of 7.\n  1044→\n  1045→#### Test: Step 7 — Review page shows all entered data correctly\n  1046→- **Initial state:** User has filled out all steps: type \"Cabin\", title \"Cozy Mountain Retreat\", address \"123 Pine Rd, Aspen, CO, USA\", 4 guests, 2 bedrooms, 2 beds, 1 bathroom, amenities \"WiFi\" and \"Kitchen\", 2 photos, price $200/night, cleaning fee $75."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01APKfpic7rdpV7eEHiTedxh","session_id":"b1ebe240-ab8e-4ccc-a035-25792ffc73c0","uuid":"f02845d5-1e1b-4e9d-add9-11105477cb8b"}
